From 4a96387550889968145e01e2a66fab99f5cf9341 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cxtjjcz <chenxiangting@huawei.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:26:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [Triton][TLA] feat: Add sparse DMA memory interfaces

Motivation: Sparse attention needs scalar UB reads, typed aliases and
runtime-strided row transfers without private code-generator adaptations.

Design: Add checked public APIs backed by native memref and HIVM builders.
Preserve source offsets, destination pitch and visible storage aliases.
Use static-capacity views with dynamic transfer subviews to support
zero-offset pointer entries, and cover the interfaces with tla_ut.

Risks: Dynamic bounds and manually scheduled buffer lifetimes remain the
caller's responsibility. Target-specific DMA constraints still apply.

Assisted-by: AI
